# AI Board NAT Controller — DNAT configuration v0.4.0 (development)
# Enabled|PublicIP|Protocol|ExternalPort|InternalIP|InternalPort
#
# Enabled: 1 (enabled), 0 (disabled; still syntax-checked).
# PublicIP: WAN_IP (validated primary WAN address) or explicit IPv4
#           routed/assigned by your ISP. Ownership is not verified.
# Protocol: tcp or udp only (lowercase).
# ExternalPort: single decimal port, 1–65535.
# InternalIP: single IPv4 address of the intended internal host.
# InternalPort: single decimal port, 1–65535; may differ from external port.
# No CIDRs, wildcards, port ranges, or leading zeroes in numeric fields.
# All six fields mandatory; no whitespace or inline comments.
# Blank lines and full-line # comments ignored.
# Enabled rules retain file order. Duplicate enabled external IP/protocol/
# port combinations are rejected after resolving WAN_IP.
# Disabled entries are not installed and do not reserve a tuple.
# Invalid input rejects the entire file; no partial rule output.
# Rules are scoped to the validated incoming WAN interface.
# No hairpin NAT, IPv6, router-local forwarding or automatic filter changes.
# DNAT can expose internal services to the Internet; verify firewall policy,
# service authentication, intended LAN destination and ISP routing first.
# Replace atomically via a sibling .new file and mv.
#
# Development stage: parser only. Existing v0.3.0 engine ignores this file.
# Do not manually install generated rules on a live router.
#
# Inactive examples using documentation addresses:
0|WAN_IP|tcp|8443|192.168.1.100|443
0|203.0.113.11|udp|51820|192.168.1.101|51820
